# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Giving Hand — Mobile App (Expo) environment template
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own values:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Expo automatically loads `.env` and exposes EXPO_PUBLIC_*
# variables to app code via process.env (SDK 49+).
# Restart `npm start` after changing values.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase project credentials ─────────────────────────────
# Create a free project at https://supabase.com, then find these
# under Project Settings → API.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

# ── Notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# • If these variables are not set, the app falls back to the
#   original project credentials hardcoded in lib/supabase.ts.
# • The "anon" key is a publishable key — safe for client code,
#   provided Row Level Security (RLS) is enabled on all tables.
# • NEVER put a service_role key here — it bypasses RLS.
# • Do not commit a real `.env`; only this template belongs in git.
